+# Alertmanager playbook (safety alerts)
+
+When an alert from aegis-safety-rules fires, follow these steps:
+
+1) CanaryPromotionHighErrorRate (critical)
+ - Check Flagger status for the canary: kubectl -n aegis get canary aegis-admission-webhook -o yaml
+ - If Flagger rolled back automatically, gather evidence: aws s3 ls s3://$EVIDENCE_BUCKET/canary_evidence/
+ - If Flagger did not rollback, run vwc_rollback.sh or set the ValidatingWebhookConfiguration to ignore.
+ - Create incident ticket and assign Infra and Product approvers.
+
+2) DPBudgetLow (warning)
+ - Notify Privacy Approver and halt new FL rounds.
+ - Run a privacy sweep: python3 services/fl/privacy_tune/dataset_tune_runner.py ...
+ - Prepare DP decision and evidence; upload to S3.
+
+3) MPCMalformedShareRateHigh (critical)
+ - Pause MPC aggregator ingress (use k8s to scale to zero).
+ - Run malicious-share tests and collect evidence.
+ - Switch to DP-first path for affected vectors.
+
